{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792449519,"nonce":"gC8kubAO79bL84qJ97j0BhuX9cU=","message":"The remaining emitters in GpuPaintContext wrote compound 3D ShapeDesc rows and tessellated mesh positions/optional vertex colours into self.batch.aux_data while their primitives used active_batch_mut(). This is reproduced by a mixed scene with unrelated static payload, polygon clips, solid/gradient meshes and a compound 3D group: before the fix, the CPU ownership guard finds routed payload appended to the static prefix, and the Metal pixel comparison fails for Dynamic, foreground=false.\n\nA second boundary case also reproduced before the fix: push a polygon in static scope, enter a motion subtree and draw a rectangle. The dynamic primitive carries ClipType::Polygon but the dynamic batch has no auxiliary rows. Merely fixing push_clip's writer is insufficient for inherited clips.\n\nThe fix routes all mesh/group payload writers through the same active-batch selection as primitives. Polygon metadata caches an offset per Static/Dynamic/Composite batch, lazily serializes inherited points on first use in a different batch, and invalidates the corresponding offsets on take_batch/take_dynamic_batch/take_composite_layer_batches. Two offset entries fit inline in SmallVec; repeated draws under a clip reuse its payload. Polygon vertex counts, odd-vertex padding and the even-odd bit survive. Composite ancestor clips remain stripped during a bake and are restored afterward. No shared ClipPath enum change is involved.\n\nGPU-free integration: 107 passed, including four routing cases for mixed payloads, inherited clips, batch drains and composite ancestor stripping. The focused run with BLINC_MULTISTOP_VERTEX=1 also passes, exercising the opt-in three-row per-vertex colour payload without changing the feature's default.\n\nOffscreen GPU tests on Apple M1 Pro / Metal: the mixed scene renders pixel-identically to static emission for dynamic and composite routes, with both foreground settings. A separate inherited-polygon pixel oracle checks red inside and white outside. Both tests pass with normal SSBO, forced VB and forced DT paths. Fallback capacities are 1024 and the multistop-vertex flag is enabled for these checks; all temporary capability overrides are restored. The 33 display-list GPU tests and the independent clip_fill_rule GPU test pass. Actual browser WebGL2 and mobile GPU pixels remain unverified. Full changed-code gate is running.\n\nAudit of adjacent existing fixes: composite_frame already uploads overlay_aux_data; its app call sites pass combined overlay aux_data. collect_canvas_overlay_from already appends canvas aux_data and rebases mesh/group/polygon offsets for both primitive lists. These existing paths are not changed in this slice.","files":null}]}